-- הסכם קיבוצי מיוחד — החלת רפורמת אופק חדש על מנהלות אשכולות גנים בחינוך
-- המיוחד (17.6.2021): from 1.9.2021 every provision of the reform agreement
-- (the agreement of 25.12.2008 as the completion agreement of 29.2.2012 and
-- later ones updated it) applies to the kindergarten cluster managers of
-- special education in the State's service, who are treated as the
-- cluster managers of ordinary education of §82 of the completion
-- agreement — save that their week is annex א's table in place of
-- §144א's, their cluster-management allowance is 25% (up to six
-- kindergartens) or 28% (seven or more) in place of §144ג(א)'s 13%, and
-- they have the special-education allowance on all their employment in
-- special education. A new manager is not an existing teacher; no benefit
-- is paid twice; the 10.1.2008 stage-one supplement ends. A one-time grant
-- of up to 26,000, in proportion to the full-time months of 1.9.2016–
-- 31.8.2021 (July and August left out, the period counting as 50 months).
--
-- §144 as §82 of the completion agreement wrote it is encoded in that
-- agreement's module, imported: what this agreement changes is written here,
-- dated, and the rest is the imported rules. The same day's agreement for
-- ordinary education (`2021-06-17_ofek-hadash_gan-cluster-managers`) is an
-- instrument of its own: this one sets its own rates, in its own words.
-- The agreement of 10.1.2008, the letters of 2.11.2016 and 19.3.2017, the
-- pension agreement of 24.8.2020 and the Women's Employment Law are not
-- encoded: what this agreement takes from them is an input, named.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `base-agreement-39`
IMPORT `2012-02-29_ofek-hadash_amendment_hascam-hashlama`

-- Salary months and calendar months are counted as one number: month m of
-- year y is y × 12 + m − 1 (convention dates.salary-month for a salary "of"
-- a month).
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the month number of` y m IS
    y TIMES 12 PLUS m MINUS 1

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the month of the year of the month number` n IS
    (n MODULO 12) PLUS 1

§ `הסכם קיבוצי מיוחד — מנהלות אשכולות גנים בחינוך המיוחד — 17.6.2021`

-- akn:preamble The agreement's frame: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:preamble/p1 The document's title; no rule.

-- The day of signing, written in by hand.
@ref akn:preamble/p2
`the signing of the special-education cluster managers' agreement` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 17 6 2021

-- akn:preamble/p3 The registration stamp under the Collective Agreements Law (12.12.2022, no. 310/2022); no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p4 A note that pages 1–5 are initialled in their margins; no rule.

-- The parties: the State, by the Treasury's wages commissioner and the
-- Ministry of Education's director-general, and the teachers' union, by its
-- secretary-general.
@ref akn:preamble/p5 akn:preamble/p6 akn:preamble/p8 akn:preamble/p9
`the special-education cluster managers' agreement's parties` MEANS LIST `the State`, `the teachers' union`

-- akn:preamble/p7 "On the one side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p10 "On the other side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p11 A recital: the reform agreements of 10.9.07 and 25.12.08; the instrument applied is named in the recital below.
-- akn:preamble/p12 A recital: the letters of 2.11.2016 and 19.3.2017 ("the letters on continuing the negotiation"), outside the corpus; §10 names them in the exhaustion.

-- The recitals define the population and the instrument applied to it: the
-- teaching employees who manage kindergarten clusters in special education
-- in the State's service, to whom the reform is applied, and the reform
-- agreement of 25.12.2008 as updated from time to time, the completion
-- agreement of 29.2.2012 included ("הסכם רפורמת אופק"), subject to this
-- agreement. That agreement's §82 is the module imported above.
@ref akn:preamble/p13 akn:preamble/p14
`the reform agreement applied was completed on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 29 2 2012

-- akn:preamble/p15 A recital: the reform changes the managers' pay structure and raises it, budgetary pensioners included; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p16 A recital: the determining salary for pension is computed by the pension agreement of 24.8.2020 ("the comprehensive pension agreement"); §9 below.

-- The recitals' two kinds of manager the Ministry had already put on the
-- reform's terms: a new teaching employee as the reform agreement defines
-- one ("a new special-education cluster manager"), and one whose pay was
-- converted under the reform before she began to manage a cluster ("one
-- converted on the eve of the signing"); grades were set for both before
-- the signing.
@ref akn:preamble/p17 akn:preamble/p18
DECLARE `special-education cluster manager's path` IS ONE OF
    `a new special-education cluster manager`
    `converted under the reform before managing the cluster`
    `on the terms before the reform`

-- akn:preamble/p19 A recital: the parties anchor what they agreed in this agreement; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p20 The words of agreement that introduce the clauses; no rule.

§§ `א. כללי`

DECLARE `part of the special-education cluster managers' agreement` IS ONE OF
    `the preamble of the special-education cluster agreement`
    `the annexes of the special-education cluster agreement`
    `the clauses of the special-education cluster agreement`

-- 1: the preamble and the annexes are an inseparable part of it.
@ref akn:art_1
GIVEN p IS A `part of the special-education cluster managers' agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `binds as the special-education cluster managers' agreement` p IF
    TRUE

#ASSERT `binds as the special-education cluster managers' agreement` `the annexes of the special-education cluster agreement`

-- 2: the headings are for convenience and do not bear on its reading.
@ref akn:art_2
GIVEN `the reading without the headings` IS A STRING, `the reading the headings suggest` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the reading the special-education cluster managers' agreement takes` `the reading without the headings` `the reading the headings suggest` IS
    `the reading without the headings`

-- 3: the masculine or the feminine is for convenience; all of it applies to
-- women and men alike.
@ref akn:art_3
`every word of the special-education cluster managers' agreement applies to women and men alike` MEANS TRUE

§§ `ב. תחולה`

@desc A teaching employee, as far as the special-education cluster managers' agreement asks who it covers.
DECLARE `special-education cluster employee` HAS
    `ranked on the teaching employees' scale, special-education cluster` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the State's service, special-education cluster`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `manages kindergarten clusters in special education`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `her path`                                                         IS A `special-education cluster manager's path`
    `converted on`                                                     IS A MAYBE DATE @desc the day her pay was converted under the reform, if it was
    `her share of a position in special-education clusters`            IS A NUMBER

-- 4: every employee on the teaching employees' scale who manages
-- kindergarten clusters in special education in the State's service — a
-- new manager, and one converted no later than the commencement, included
-- ("מנהלות אשכולות גנים בחנ"מ") — for the part of her position in
-- special-education clusters.
@ref akn:art_4
GIVEN e IS A `special-education cluster employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a special-education cluster manager` e IF
        e's `ranked on the teaching employees' scale, special-education cluster`
    AND e's `in the State's service, special-education cluster`
    AND e's `manages kindergarten clusters in special education`

GIVEN e IS A `special-education cluster employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the share of her position the special-education cluster agreement reaches` e IS
    IF `a special-education cluster manager` e
    THEN e's `her share of a position in special-education clusters`
    ELSE 0

§§ `ג. תחילה`

-- 5: it begins on 1.9.21 ("the commencement").
@ref akn:art_5
`the commencement of the special-education cluster managers' agreement` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2021

§§ `ד. החלת הסכם רפורמת אופק על מנהלות אשכולות גנים בחנ"מ`

-- 6: from the commencement every provision of the reform agreement applies
-- to them, subject to (א)–(ה).
@ref akn:art_6
GIVEN e IS A `special-education cluster employee`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reform agreement applies to her under the special-education cluster agreement` e d IF
    `a special-education cluster manager` e AND d `is on or after` `the commencement of the special-education cluster managers' agreement`

-- (א): for applying the reform agreement, the salary conversion included,
-- she is treated as a cluster manager of §82 of the completion agreement
-- ("a cluster manager in ordinary education").
DECLARE `cluster manager as the reform agreement treats her` IS ONE OF
    `a cluster manager in ordinary education, of §82`
    `not a cluster manager under the reform`

@ref akn:art_6__para_a
GIVEN e IS A `special-education cluster employee`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `cluster manager as the reform agreement treats her`
DECIDE `how the reform agreement treats a special-education cluster manager` e d IS
    IF `the reform agreement applies to her under the special-education cluster agreement` e d
    THEN `a cluster manager in ordinary education, of §82`
    ELSE `not a cluster manager under the reform`

-- akn:art_6__para_b The opening of (ב): notwithstanding (א), (1)–(3) for the special-education cluster managers.

-- (ב)(1): annex א's table takes the place of §144א's: her week by the
-- number of kindergartens in the cluster. The annex's table is below; the
-- completion agreement's week is imported.
@ref akn:art_6__para_b__subpara_1
GIVEN kindergartens IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `cluster manager's week`
DECIDE `a special-education cluster manager's week` kindergartens d IS
    IF d `is on or after` `the commencement of the special-education cluster managers' agreement`
    THEN `the week annex א of the special-education cluster agreement gives` kindergartens
    ELSE `a kindergarten cluster manager's week` kindergartens

-- (ב)(2): §144ג(א) reads, for them: (1) up to 6 kindergartens, a
-- special-education cluster-management allowance of 25% of the combined
-- salary; (2) 7 or more, 28%. "עד 6" counts whole kindergartens and the
-- next row opens at 7, so 6 is in the first row (recorded under
-- thresholds.until's exceptions). Before the commencement, §144ג(א)'s 13%.
@ref akn:art_6__para_b__subpara_2
GIVEN kindergartens IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the special-education cluster-management allowance rate` kindergartens d IS
    IF d `is on or after` `the commencement of the special-education cluster managers' agreement`
    THEN (IF kindergartens AT MOST 6 THEN 25% ELSE 28%)
    ELSE `the cluster-management allowance rate`

-- ¶2: §144ג(ב)–(ד) apply: the higher of the allowance and a trailing one
-- ((ד)); the State acts to have the allowance, as (2) amends it, recognised
-- as a fixed supplement for the State Service (Pensions) Law ((ב)); for one
-- insured in an accrual pension, contributions on it.
@ref akn:art_6__para_b__subpara_2/p2
GIVEN kindergartens IS A NUMBER, `combined salary` IS A NUMBER, `the trailing allowance` IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the special-education cluster-management allowance` kindergartens `combined salary` `the trailing allowance` d IS
    max (`the special-education cluster-management allowance rate` kindergartens d TIMES `combined salary`) `the trailing allowance`

@ref akn:art_6__para_b__subpara_2/p2
`recognising the special-education cluster-management allowance for pension` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `act to recognise the cluster-management allowance as a fixed supplement for the pensions law`

@ref akn:art_6__para_b__subpara_2/p2
GIVEN `insured in an accrual pension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `accrual-pension contributions are made on the special-education cluster allowance` `insured in an accrual pension` IF
    `insured in an accrual pension`

#ASSERT `the special-education cluster-management allowance rate` 6 `the commencement of the special-education cluster managers' agreement` EQUALS 25%
#ASSERT `the special-education cluster-management allowance` 9 10000 0 `the commencement of the special-education cluster managers' agreement` EQUALS 2800
#ASSERT `the special-education cluster-management allowance rate` 9 (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2021) EQUALS 13%

-- (ב)(3): the special-education allowance on the whole of her employment
-- in special education — not, as §39(ג) has it for a teacher in ordinary
-- and special-education classes, on the share of her frontal hours there.
-- The allowance's rate is the base agreement's, as later agreements set it,
-- an input.
@ref akn:art_6__para_b__subpara_3
GIVEN `the special-education allowance rate` IS A NUMBER, `full-position combined salary` IS A NUMBER, `her share of a position in special education` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a special-education cluster manager's special-education allowance` `the special-education allowance rate` `full-position combined salary` `her share of a position in special education` IS
    `the special-education allowance rate` TIMES `full-position combined salary` TIMES `her share of a position in special education`

-- A manager of 4 kindergartens, the whole position in special education: 22
-- of her 34 hours are with the children. §39(ג) would count the frontal
-- hours' share; (ב)(3) counts all of it.
`a cluster week by §39(ג)` MEANS
    `allowance case` WITH
        `full-position combined salary` IS 10000
        `position fraction`             IS 1
        `frontal hours`                 IS 22
        `frontal hours in special-education classes` IS 22
#ASSERT `a special-education cluster manager's special-education allowance` (14%) 10000 1 EQUALS 1400
#ASSERT `the special-education position` `a cluster week by §39(ג)` EQUALS 1

-- (ג): a new special-education cluster manager is not, by this agreement,
-- an "existing teaching employee" or an "existing kindergarten teacher".
@ref akn:art_6__para_c
GIVEN p IS A `special-education cluster manager's path`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this agreement makes her an existing teaching employee or kindergarten teacher` p IF
    FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `this agreement makes her an existing teaching employee or kindergarten teacher` `a new special-education cluster manager`

-- (ד): no right, payment or benefit twice under this agreement, where it
-- was already given for the same period before the commencement; no
-- provision of the reform agreement applied again where it already was.
@ref akn:art_6__para_d
GIVEN `already given for the same period before the commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this agreement gives the benefit` `already given for the same period before the commencement` IF
    NOT `already given for the same period before the commencement`

-- ¶2, for example and not to exhaust it: a new manager, and one converted
-- before the commencement whose grade was already set, is not converted as
-- an "existing kindergarten teacher" under §140 or §144; and one already
-- entitled to age hours on the eve of the commencement has none by this
-- agreement (and keeps what she had).
@ref akn:art_6__para_d/p2
GIVEN p IS A `special-education cluster manager's path`, `her grade was set before the commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `converted as an existing kindergarten teacher under §140 or §144` p `her grade was set before the commencement` IF
        p EQUALS `on the terms before the reform`
    AND NOT `her grade was set before the commencement`

@ref akn:art_6__para_d/p2
GIVEN `entitled to age hours on the eve of the commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this agreement gives her age hours` `entitled to age hours on the eve of the commencement` IF
    NOT `entitled to age hours on the eve of the commencement`

#ASSERT NOT `converted as an existing kindergarten teacher under §140 or §144` `a new special-education cluster manager` TRUE
#ASSERT `converted as an existing kindergarten teacher under §140 or §144` `on the terms before the reform` FALSE

-- (ה): §3 of the special agreement of 10.1.2008 (entry to stage one of the
-- reform) does not apply to them from the reform's application; from
-- 1.9.2021 at the latest no manager on the reform's terms under this
-- agreement has its supplement. The agreement of 10.1.2008 is not encoded;
-- its supplement is an input where it is paid.
@ref akn:art_6__para_e
GIVEN `on the reform's terms under this agreement` IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the stage-one supplement of 10.1.2008 is paid to a special-education cluster manager` `on the reform's terms under this agreement` d IF
    NOT (`on the reform's terms under this agreement` AND d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2021))

#ASSERT NOT `the stage-one supplement of 10.1.2008 is paid to a special-education cluster manager` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2021)

§§ `7 מענק חד פעמי`

-- akn:art_7 The clause's heading, "a one-time grant"; its rules are (א)–(יב).

`the grant period starts` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016
`the grant period ends` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2021
`the one-time grant of the special-education cluster agreement` MEANS 26000
`the grant period counts as months` MEANS 50

-- The months that count toward the grant: July and August are left out
-- ((ב)–(ד)), so the period of 1.9.2016–31.8.2021 counts as 50.
GIVEN `from year` IS A NUMBER, `from month` IS A NUMBER, `to year` IS A NUMBER, `to month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the months counted for the special-education grant from` `from year` `from month` `to` `to year` `to month` IS
    count (filter (GIVEN n YIELD `not July or August` n) (range (`the month number of` `from year` `from month`) (`the month number of` `to year` `to month`)))
    WHERE
        GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        DECIDE `not July or August` n IF
            `the month of the year of the month number` n LESS THAN 7 OR `the month of the year of the month number` n GREATER THAN 8

#ASSERT `the months counted for the special-education grant from` 2016 9 `to` 2021 8 EQUALS `the grant period counts as months`

DECLARE `absence in the grant period` IS ONE OF
    `at work in the role`
    `on unpaid leave, or leave treated as unpaid`
    `on unpaid leave after maternity and parenthood`
    `in reserve duty`
    `in maternity and parenthood`
    `on unpaid sick leave`

@desc A stretch of the grant period at one share of a position, in the role.
DECLARE `stretch of the special-education grant period` HAS
    `relevant months in the stretch` IS A NUMBER @desc months of the stretch, July and August left out
    `share of a position in the stretch, special-education grant` IS A NUMBER @desc for an absence of (ז), the share on the eve of it
    `what the manager was doing in the stretch` IS A `absence in the grant period`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, share IS A NUMBER, a IS AN `absence in the grant period`
GIVETH A `stretch of the special-education grant period`
DECIDE `a special-education grant stretch of` n share a IS
    `stretch of the special-education grant period` WITH
        `relevant months in the stretch` IS n
        `share of a position in the stretch, special-education grant` IS share
        `what the manager was doing in the stretch` IS a

-- (ה)–(ו): unpaid leave, or leave treated as unpaid — after the maternity
-- and parenthood period too — does not count; reserve duty, maternity and
-- parenthood (26 weeks, by §6 of the Women's Employment Law) and unpaid
-- sick leave do. (ז): a month of these absences counts at the share of a
-- position on their eve. (ח): (ו)–(ז) apply to a man as well.
@ref akn:art_7__para_e akn:art_7__para_f akn:art_7__para_g akn:art_7__para_h
GIVEN a IS AN `absence in the grant period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a stretch counts toward the special-education grant` a IF
        NOT a EQUALS `on unpaid leave, or leave treated as unpaid`
    AND NOT a EQUALS `on unpaid leave after maternity and parenthood`

-- (ג), (ד), (ז) ¶2: a month's share of a position above 100% counts as
-- 100%.
@ref akn:art_7__para_c akn:art_7__para_g/p2
GIVEN s IS A `stretch of the special-education grant period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the full-position months of a special-education grant stretch` s IS
    IF `a stretch counts toward the special-education grant` (s's `what the manager was doing in the stretch`)
    THEN s's `relevant months in the stretch` TIMES min (s's `share of a position in the stretch, special-education grant`) 1
    ELSE 0

-- (א): a special-education cluster manager at the commencement who was in
-- the role in a full position throughout 1.9.2016–31.8.2021 has a one-time
-- grant of 26,000. (ב)–(ד): one in a full position for part of it, in a
-- part position for all of it, or both, has the share of the grant her
-- full-position months are of the 50 the period counts as.
@ref akn:art_7__para_a akn:art_7__para_b akn:art_7__para_d
GIVEN `a special-education cluster manager at the commencement` IS A BOOLEAN, stretches IS A LIST OF `stretch of the special-education grant period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the special-education cluster manager's one-time grant` `a special-education cluster manager at the commencement` stretches IS
    IF `a special-education cluster manager at the commencement`
    THEN `the one-time grant of the special-education cluster agreement`
         TIMES min 1 (sum (map `the full-position months of a special-education grant stretch` stretches) DIVIDED BY `the grant period counts as months`)
    ELSE 0

#ASSERT `the special-education cluster manager's one-time grant` TRUE (LIST `a special-education grant stretch of` 50 1 `at work in the role`) EQUALS 26000

-- (ב), the example: full time from 1.9.2016 to 31.3.2020 — three years of
-- ten months and the seven of September 2019 to March 2020, 37 — has
-- 37 × 26,000 / 50 = 19,240.
@ref akn:art_7__para_b/p2 akn:art_7__para_b/p3 akn:art_7__para_b/p4 akn:art_7__para_b/p5
`the example of (ב)` MEANS
    LIST `a special-education grant stretch of` (`the months counted for the special-education grant from` 2016 9 `to` 2020 3) 1 `at work in the role`

#ASSERT `the months counted for the special-education grant from` 2016 9 `to` 2020 3 EQUALS 37
#ASSERT `the special-education cluster manager's one-time grant` TRUE `the example of (ב)` EQUALS 19240

-- (ד), the example: 1.9.2017–31.8.2018 at 100% (10 months), 1.9.2018–
-- 31.8.2019 at 110%, counted as 100% (10), 1.9.2019–31.1.2020 at 70% (5):
-- (10 + 10 + 5 × 0.7) × 26,000 / 50 = 12,220.
@ref akn:art_7__para_d/p2 akn:art_7__para_d__subpara_1 akn:art_7__para_d__subpara_2 akn:art_7__para_d__subpara_3 akn:art_7__para_d/p3 akn:art_7__para_d/p4 akn:art_7__para_d/p5 akn:art_7__para_d/p6 akn:art_7__para_d/p7 akn:art_7__para_d/p8 akn:art_7__para_d/p9 akn:art_7__para_d/p10
`the example of (ד)` MEANS
    LIST `a special-education grant stretch of` (`the months counted for the special-education grant from` 2017 9 `to` 2018 8) 1 `at work in the role`,
         `a special-education grant stretch of` (`the months counted for the special-education grant from` 2018 9 `to` 2019 8) 1.1 `at work in the role`,
         `a special-education grant stretch of` (`the months counted for the special-education grant from` 2019 9 `to` 2020 1) 0.7 `at work in the role`

#ASSERT `the special-education cluster manager's one-time grant` TRUE `the example of (ד)` EQUALS 12220

-- A year of unpaid leave adds nothing; a year of maternity at the eve's
-- 80% adds 8 full-position months.
#ASSERT `the special-education cluster manager's one-time grant` TRUE (LIST `a special-education grant stretch of` 10 1 `on unpaid leave, or leave treated as unpaid`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the special-education cluster manager's one-time grant` TRUE (LIST `a special-education grant stretch of` 10 0.8 `in maternity and parenthood`) EQUALS 26000 TIMES 8 DIVIDED BY 50

DECLARE `special-education grant purpose` IS ONE OF
    `salary for every purpose, special-education grant`
    `the hour value, and the pay for unique hours such as kindergarten activity hours`
    `the salary reduction for an hour of absence, special-education grant`
    `the payment under §33(ד), special-education grant`
    `severance pay, special-education grant`
    `provident-fund contributions, special-education grant`
    `topping up to the minimum wage, special-education grant`
    `the salary base of the combined-salary tables`

-- (ט)–(יא): the grant is not salary for any purpose; it counts for none of
-- these, no contributions are made on it, it is not in topping up to the
-- minimum wage, and it does not change the salary base of the tables.
@ref akn:art_7__para_i akn:art_7__para_j akn:art_7__para_ja
GIVEN p IS A `special-education grant purpose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the special-education cluster grant counts for` p IF
    FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `the special-education cluster grant counts for` `topping up to the minimum wage, special-education grant`

DECLARE `special-education grant absence at payment` IS ONE OF
    `at work at the payment`
    `on unpaid leave at the payment`
    `on unpaid sick leave at the payment`
    `in maternity and parenthood at the payment`
    `absent for a work injury not charged to sick leave, at the payment`

-- (יב): a manager entitled to the grant who, when it is paid under §8, is
-- away for one of (1)–(4), is paid it in the first salary paid on her
-- return, or at the latest the next. F-ofek-hadash-gan-cluster-se-2021-a:
-- the opening speaks of "one of (1) to (5)"; (יב) lists four. The four
-- listed are read (convention reading.misprint).
@ref akn:art_7__para_jb akn:art_7__para_jb__subpara_1 akn:art_7__para_jb__subpara_2 akn:art_7__para_jb__subpara_3 akn:art_7__para_jb__subpara_4
GIVEN a IS A `special-education grant absence at payment`, `the latest salary month of §8` IS A NUMBER, `the first salary month on her return` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the last salary month the special-education grant may be paid in` a `the latest salary month of §8` `the first salary month on her return` IS
    IF a EQUALS `at work at the payment`
    THEN `the latest salary month of §8`
    ELSE `the first salary month on her return` PLUS 1

`the circumstances (יב) lists` MEANS LIST "(1)", "(2)", "(3)", "(4)"
`(יב) opens on circumstances (1) to (5) and lists four` MEANS
    NOT elem "(5)" `the circumstances (יב) lists`
#ASSERT `(יב) opens on circumstances (1) to (5) and lists four`

§§ `8 מועדי תשלום`

-- 8: what §§6 and 7 give is paid from the salary of September 2021 (paid
-- in October), at the latest in the salary of October 2021 (paid in
-- November), with the arrears from the commencement.
@ref akn:art_8 akn:art_8/p1
`the first salary month that pays the special-education cluster agreement` MEANS `the month number of` 2021 9
`the latest salary month that pays the special-education cluster agreement` MEANS `the month number of` 2021 10

#ASSERT `the last salary month the special-education grant may be paid in` `at work at the payment` `the latest salary month that pays the special-education cluster agreement` 0 EQUALS `the month number of` 2021 10

§§ `ה. הסכם הפנסיה הכולל`

-- 9: for the comprehensive pension agreement of 24.8.2020 (outside the
-- corpus), this agreement is "another collective agreement" in its
-- definition of "the terms of the Ofek Hadash reform" (its §4).
@ref akn:art_9
`the special-education cluster agreement is another collective agreement for the pension agreement of 24.8.2020` MEANS TRUE

§§ `ו. מיצוי תביעות`

DECLARE `special-education cluster claim action` IS ONE OF
    `raise a claim on applying the reform to the special-education cluster managers`
    `negotiate further economic demands for applying the reform to them`
    `strike or lock out over a matter of §§10–13 of the special-education cluster agreement`

-- 10–12: it fully exhausts the parties' claims on applying the reform to
-- these managers — under §155(ב) of the reform agreement, the letters on
-- continuing the negotiation and §90 of the completion agreement included,
-- and fully on the change of their work and its price; no further economic
-- demands are negotiated.
@ref akn:art_10 akn:art_11 akn:art_12
`no further claims on the special-education cluster managers` MEANS
    (PARTY `the teachers' union`
     SHANT `raise a claim on applying the reform to the special-education cluster managers`)
    RAND
    (PARTY `the teachers' union`
     SHANT `negotiate further economic demands for applying the reform to them`)

-- 13: because of 6(א), exhaustion provisions that future agreements set on
-- updating the reform agreement for ordinary-education cluster managers
-- apply to these managers too, unless the parties agree otherwise.
@ref akn:art_13
GIVEN `the future agreement's exhaustion reaches ordinary-education cluster managers` IS A BOOLEAN, `the parties agreed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a future exhaustion reaches the special-education cluster managers` `the future agreement's exhaustion reaches ordinary-education cluster managers` `the parties agreed otherwise` IF
    `the future agreement's exhaustion reaches ordinary-education cluster managers` AND NOT `the parties agreed otherwise`

-- 14: the exhaustion provisions that bind the parties stand.
@ref akn:art_14
`the special-education cluster agreement takes away from the exhaustion provisions already binding` MEANS FALSE

§§ `ז. שקט תעשייתי`

-- 15: neither party takes a strike or lockout, or other organised harm to
-- the work, over a matter of §§10–13; 16: the industrial-peace provisions
-- that bind the parties stand.
@ref akn:art_15 akn:art_16
`industrial peace under the special-education cluster agreement` MEANS
    (PARTY `the State`
     SHANT `strike or lock out over a matter of §§10–13 of the special-education cluster agreement`)
    RAND
    (PARTY `the teachers' union`
     SHANT `strike or lock out over a matter of §§10–13 of the special-education cluster agreement`)

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:conclusions/p1 "In witness whereof"; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p2 The signatures; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/t1 The parties' signature headings; no rule.
-- akn:attachments The annexes: a label row with no text of its own.

§§ `נספח א' — טבלת מבנה השבוע של מנהלת אשכול גנים בחנ"מ`

-- Annex א: by the kindergartens in the cluster, the frontal, enrichment or
-- reinforcement hours with the children, the cluster's management hours,
-- and the total. Its last row is "10 או 11"; it has no row below 4 or above
-- 11, and gives none (as §144א's table, F-ofek-hadash-hashlama-2012-j;
-- convention thresholds.missing-row). The week is the completion
-- agreement's `cluster manager's week`.
@desc A row of annex א of the special-education cluster agreement.
DECLARE `row of the special-education cluster week table` HAS
    `kindergartens the row is for`       IS A LIST OF NUMBER
    `the row's week`                      IS A `cluster manager's week`
    `the row's printed total`             IS A NUMBER

GIVEN ks IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the first number of` ks IS
    CONSIDER ks
    WHEN k FOLLOWED BY rest THEN k
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0

GIVEN children IS A NUMBER, management IS A NUMBER, total IS A NUMBER
      ks IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A `row of the special-education cluster week table`
DECIDE `a special-education cluster row` children management total ks IS
    `row of the special-education cluster week table` WITH
        `kindergartens the row is for` IS ks
        `the row's week`               IS `cluster manager's week` WITH
                                              `hours with the children`    IS children
                                              `hours managing the cluster` IS management
        `the row's printed total`      IS total

@ref akn:att_1__hc_1 akn:att_1__hc_1/t1
`annex א of the special-education cluster agreement` MEANS
    LIST `a special-education cluster row` 22 12 34 (LIST 4),
         `a special-education cluster row` 19 15 34 (LIST 5),
         `a special-education cluster row` 16 18 34 (LIST 6),
         `a special-education cluster row` 13 21 34 (LIST 7),
         `a special-education cluster row` 10 24 34 (LIST 8),
         `a special-education cluster row` 7 27 34 (LIST 9),
         `a special-education cluster row` 4 30 34 (LIST 10, 11)

-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p2 The annex's file number (2019-17870); no rule.

GIVEN kindergartens IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `cluster manager's week`
DECIDE `the week annex א of the special-education cluster agreement gives` kindergartens IS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN r YIELD elem kindergartens (r's `kindergartens the row is for`)) `annex א of the special-education cluster agreement`
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (r's `the row's week`)
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING

-- Every row's two columns make up the total it prints, the 34 hours of the
-- position base (§144א(א), imported).
#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD `hours of a cluster manager's week` (r's `the row's week`) EQUALS r's `the row's printed total`) `annex א of the special-education cluster agreement`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the row's printed total` EQUALS `a kindergarten cluster manager's position base`) `annex א of the special-education cluster agreement`
-- Each further kindergarten moves three hours from the children to the
-- cluster's management (two in §144א's table).
#ASSERT map (GIVEN r YIELD `the first number of` (r's `kindergartens the row is for`)) `annex א of the special-education cluster agreement` EQUALS LIST 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10
#ASSERT (    `hours with the children in` (`a special-education cluster manager's week` 4 `the commencement of the special-education cluster managers' agreement`)
         EQUALS JUST 22)
#ASSERT (    `hours with the children in` (`a special-education cluster manager's week` 4 (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2021))
         EQUALS JUST 26)
#ASSERT `hours with the children in` (`a special-education cluster manager's week` 11 `the commencement of the special-education cluster managers' agreement`) EQUALS JUST 4
#ASSERT `a special-education cluster manager's week` 12 `the commencement of the special-education cluster managers' agreement` EQUALS NOTHING
